cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PatBiNN: Hierarchical Binarized Virus Read Classifier"
message: "If you use this software, please cite the paper below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Harary
    given-names: Yuval
  - family-names: Sharoni
    given-names: Almog
  - family-names: Garzón
    given-names: Esteban
  - family-names: Yavits
    given-names: Leonid
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/yuval93813/patbinn"
abstract: >-
  A hardware-oriented binarized neural network that classifies a single short
  Illumina sequencing read into one of 58 virus variants, using a two-stage
  Mixture-of-Experts design (a family router followed by one of eight per-family
  variant experts). Evaluated with genome-level 5-fold cross-validation on 543
  real NCBI isolates.
keywords:
  - binarized neural networks
  - processing-in-memory
  - genome classification
  - metagenomics
  - mixture of experts
